     \cf22 \cb23  27 +\cf9 This installs dependencies, seeds 8 representative tickers (SPY, QQQ, AAPL,                                                                                                                                                                                  \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  28 +\cf9 NVDA, TSLA, META, GLD, TLT), and launches Streamlit. Your browser opens on                                                                                                                                                                                   \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  29 +\cf9 the Discover page and you immediately see real data.                                                                                                                                                                                                         \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  30 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  31 +\cf9 **Prerequisites:** Python 3.11 or newer. That's it \'97 no API keys, no database                                                                                                                                                                                \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  32 +\cf9 setup, no manual configuration. Yahoo Finance is the only external data                                                                                                                                                                                      \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  33 +\cf9 source and it's public.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  34 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  35 +\cf9 ### What you don't need                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  36 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  37 +\cf9 - No API keys (Yahoo is public)                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  38 +\cf9 - No database installation (DuckDB is embedded, single file)                                                                                                                                                                                                 \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  39 +\cf9 - No migration scripts                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  40 +\cf9 - No manual config files                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  41 +\cf9 - No pre-loaded dataset                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  42 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  43 +\cf9 ### After Quick Start                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  44 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  45 +\cf9 Once the app is running you have three ways to expand the universe:                                                                                                                                                                                          \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  46 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  47 +\cf9 1. **Sidebar "Add ticker" box** \'97 type any Yahoo symbol, hit Add, it resolves                                                                                                                                                                                \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  48 +\cf9    and backfills 2 years of history in seconds. Supports international codes:                                                                                                                                                                                \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  49 +\cf9    `1810` auto-resolves to `1810.HK` (Xiaomi on Hong Kong), `LLOY` to `LLOY.L`                                                                                                                                                                               \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  50 +\cf9    (Lloyds on London), etc.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  51 +\cf9 2. **Sidebar "Live screener \'97 bulk load"** \'97 one click loads all 280+ tickers                                                                                                                                                                                \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  52 +\cf9    in the curated universe. Takes ~5-10 minutes depending on Yahoo throttling.                                                                                                                                                                               \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  53 +\cf9 3. **`make seed-full`** from the terminal \'97 same as option 2 but non-interactive.                                                                                                                                                                            \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  54 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  55 +\cf9 ## Available Make Targets                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  56 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  57 +\cf9 | Target | What it does |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  58 +\cf9 |---|---|                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  59 +\cf9 | `make quickstart` | **Everything.** Install deps + 8-ticker seed + start UI. Run this first. |                                                                                                                                                             \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  60 +\cf9 | `make setup` | Install Python dependencies only. |                                                                                                                                                                                                         \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  61 +\cf9 | `make run` | Start the Streamlit UI (assumes you already have data). |                                                                                                                                                                                     \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  62 +\cf9 | `make seed-starter` | Seed the 8-ticker starter pack. Same as the seed step in `quickstart`. |                                                                                                                                                             \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  63 +\cf9 | `make seed-full` | Seed the entire curated universe (~280 tickers, ~5-10 min). |                                                                                                                                                                           \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  64 +\cf9 | `make seed` | Alias for `seed-full` (kept for compatibility with cron). |                                                                                                                                                                                  \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  65 +\cf9 | `make scrape` | Live options chain scrape \'97 updates real IV for every loaded ticker. Intended for cron. |                                                                                                                                                  \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  66 +\cf9 | `make test` | Run the full pytest suite (240+ tests). |                                                                                                                                                                                                    \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  67 +\cf9 | `make verify` | Run the 4-gate verification: spec conformance, regression, golden values, runtime smoke. |                                                                                                                                                 \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  68 +\cf9 | `make clean` | Delete the local database. |                                                                                                                                                                                                                \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  69 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  70 +\cf9 ## Daily Data Refresh                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  71 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  72 +\cf9 VolScope distinguishes **historical backfill** (HV from Yahoo OHLCV) from                                                                                                                                                                                    \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  73 +\cf9 **live IV** (today's options chain). `make quickstart` only does the                                                                                                                                                                                         \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  74 +\cf9 historical backfill \'97 it gives you 2 years of HV data with a YZ \'d7 1.12 VRP                                                                                                                                                                                   \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  75 +\cf9 proxy for the IV column. To get real options-chain IV, run:                                                                                                                                                                                                  \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  76 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  77 +\cf9 ```bash                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  78 +\cf9 make scrape                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  79 +\cf9 ```                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  80 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  81 +\cf9 Or wire it into cron:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  82 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  83 +\cf9 ```                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  84 +\cf9 30 16 * * 1-5 cd /path/to/volscope && /usr/bin/make scrape                                                                                                                                                                                                   \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  85 +\cf9 ```                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  86 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  87 +\cf9 (4:30pm on weekdays, after US market close.)                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  88 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf12  89\cf2  \cf9  ##\cf2  \cf9 Architecture\cf2 \
