\f1\b (\cf10 sector_rotation.py\cf2 )
\f0\b0 \
\
 1. \cf10 compute_sector_aggregates(daily_vol_df)\cf2  \'97 Gruppierung nach (sector, date), Median IV/Perc/HV, Mean PCR, Total OI/Vol\
 2. \cf10 compute_sector_momentum(agg,\cf2  \cf10 windows=[5,10,21])\cf2  \'97 Rolling Momentum: \cf10 perc_delta\cf2 , \cf10 iv_momentum\cf2 , \cf10 oi_momentum\cf2  pro Window\
 3. \cf10 classify_sector_regime(agg,\cf2  \cf10 lookback=252)\cf2  \'97 HOT/COLD/NEUTRAL via z-score (reuse \cf10 vol_regime\cf2  Pattern aus \cf10 vol_metrics.py\cf2 ), plus HEATING/COOLING/STABLE Trend\
 4. \cf10 compute_rotation_matrix(regimes,\cf2  \cf10 lag=21)\cf2  \'97 Markov-\'e4hnliche Transition-Probabilities: "Wenn Energy HOT wird, welcher Sektor folgt historisch innerhalb 21 Tagen?"\
 5. \cf10 get_current_rotation_snapshot(regimes,\cf2  \cf10 matrix)\cf2  \'97 Identifiziert aktuell HEATING Sektoren + predicts "who's next"\
