     \cf22 \cb23  125 +\cf9 ## Where the DB Lives                                                                                                                                                                                                     \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf12  126\cf2  \cf9  \cf2 \
     \cf20 \cb21   61 -\cf9 ```                                                                                                                                                                                                                       \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf20 \cb21   62 -\cf9 30 16 * * 1-5 cd /path/to/volscope && /usr/bin/make scrape                                                                                                                                                                \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf20 \cb21   63 -\cf9 ```                                                                                                                                                                                                                       \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  127 +\cf9 | Platform | Default path |                                                                                                                                                                                               \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  128 +\cf9 |---|---|                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  129 +\cf9 | macOS | `~/Library/Application Support/VolScope/volscope.db` |                                                                                                                                                          \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  130 +\cf9 | Linux | `$XDG_DATA_HOME/volscope/volscope.db` (or `~/.local/share/volscope/...`) |                                                                                                                                      \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  131 +\cf9 | Override | Set `VOLSCOPE_DATA_DIR=/some/path` in `.env` or the shell. |                                                                                                                                                 \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf12  132\cf2  \cf9  \cf2 \
     \cf22 \cb23  133 +\cf9 The DB location is outside the project directory on purpose: macOS `fileprovi`                                                                                                                                            \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  134 +\cf9 (iCloud File Provider) grabs write handles on anything under `~/Desktop`,                                                                                                                                                 \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  135 +\cf9 which collides with DuckDB's exclusive lock. Keeping the DB in                                                                                                                                                            \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  136 +\cf9 Application Support avoids that.                                                                                                                                                                                          \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  137 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                           \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  138 +\cf9 ## Troubleshooting                                                                                                                                                                                                        \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  139 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                           \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  140 +\cf9 **"Legacy seed data detected" banner on Scope.** Your DB has rows from a                                                                                                                                                  \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  141 +\cf9 pre-v1.0 seed where `iv_30d == hv_20d` (flat zero spread). Click the                                                                                                                                                      \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  142 +\cf9 **Fix now** button in the banner, or **Fix all tickers** for a full                                                                                                                                                       \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  143 +\cf9 migration. No CLI / restart needed.                                                                                                                                                                                       \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  144 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                           \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  145 +\cf9 **"Database unavailable" on startup.** Another VolScope process is holding                                                                                                                                                \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  146 +\cf9 the DuckDB write lock. Usually a stale `streamlit run` or a running                                                                                                                                                       \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  147 +\cf9 `make scrape`. Stop it and reload.                                                                                                                                                                                        \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  148 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                           \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  149 +\cf9 **SPY IV looks wrong (> 50%).** An old scraper run with broken ATM                                                                                                                                                        \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  150 +\cf9 interpolation. The scrape sanity layer now rejects IV > 120% for broad ETFs                                                                                                                                               \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  151 +\cf9 and > 500% for single names. Run `make scrape` once and the stale row gets                                                                                                                                                \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  152 +\cf9 overwritten with the corrected value.                                                                                                                                                                                     \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf22 \cb23  153 +\cf9                                                                                                                                                                                                                           \cf2 \cb1 \
